- The radius of the ${}_{7}^{15} \mathrm{~N}$ nucleus is $1 \mathrm{fm}$.
- The radius of the ${}_{8}^{15} \mathrm{O}$ nucleus is $1 \mathrm{fm}$.
- The binding energy of the ${}_{7}^{15} \mathrm{~N}$ nucleus is $931.5 \mathrm{MeV} / c^{2}$.
- The binding energy of the ${}_{8}^{15} \mathrm{O}$ nucleus is $15.003065 \mathrm{MeV} / c^{2}$.

The difference in binding energies is given by:
\[
\Delta E = \Delta E_{7}^{15} - \Delta E_{8}^{15} = 931.5 \mathrm{MeV} - 15.003065 \mathrm{MeV} = 931.0 \mathrm{MeV}
\]

The electrostatic energy of the nucleus is:
\[
E = \frac{3}{5} \frac{Z(Z-1) e^{2}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}
\]

